{% /aside %}

To map the distribution of samples across a dataset.

## Steps

1. Select `Sequences` in the navigation bar {% ref id="A" /%}.
2. Open `Extract and map sequence IDs` from the tool list on wide windows, or select the tool name {% ref id="B" /%} at the top of the page to switch tools.
3. Add the input files {% ref id="C" /%} with `Browse files`, `Browse folder`, or `Open archive`. SEGUI searches a folder and its subfolders for files that match the tool's input format. See [file input](/docs/gui-usage/intro/#file-input) for mobile options.
4. Select `Browse` under `Select output directory` to choose the output folder. On phones and tablets, enter a `Directory name` instead; SEGUI saves it in the app's own folder.
5. Add prefix for the output files.
6. Turn on `Map sequence ID` (**important**).
7. Select the run button {% ref id="D" /%}, labeled `Extract ID`, to start the task.

## Output

The app will generate two files:

- **Unique IDs**: A list of unique IDs in your dataset (default name: `id.txt`).
- **ID Map**: A csv file containing the distribution of your samples presented in TRUE/FALSE values across your alignments (default name: `id_map.txt`)

ID map file will look like as below:

| Alignments | sequence_1 | sequence_2 | sequence_3 |
| ---------- | ---------- | ---------- | ---------- |
| locus_1    | TRUE       | FALSE      | TRUE       |
| locus_2    | TRUE       | TRUE       | TRUE       |
| locus_3    | FALSE      | FALSE      | TRUE       |
